{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the children of Israel.</b> He set His heart to contemplate the distress of their bondage — as you say: 'and I will see the blood.'" "<b>And Elohim knew.</b> In the sense of 'you shall know the face of your flock' (Proverbs 27:23) — He prepared His heart and His compassion to know their distress. Another interpretation: <b>And Elohim saw the children of Israel</b> — what was being done to them openly. <b>And Elohim knew.</b> What was being done to them in secret. And so our Rabbis said: 'and He saw our affliction' — this is separation. Another interpretation: as it is written <b>and Elohim knew</b> — this thing no person knew about another; only HaKadosh Barukh Hu, for hidden things are His."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:54.792706772Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}